hadiths[260]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18660","Waki narrated to us, my father and Israil narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say on the day of Hunayn: I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib."
"18661","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from al-Hakam, he said: So Ibn Abi Layla narrated it to me, he said: So he narrated that al-Bara ibn Azib said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prayed - bowing, and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he prostrated, and when he raised his head from prostration, and between the two prostrations - was nearly equal."
"18662","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to us that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to observe qunut in the Fajr and Maghrib prayers; Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It is not narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he observed qunut in Maghrib except in this hadith, and from Ali his saying."
"18663","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani say: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came from Makkah to Madinah, he said: Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum followed him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against him, and his horse sank with him, so he said: Supplicate Allah for me and I shall not harm you; he said: So he supplicated Allah for him; he said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, thirsted, and they passed by a shepherd of sheep, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, said: So I took a cup and milked into it for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a portion of milk, and I brought it to him, and he drank until I was satisfied."
"18664","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Ubaydah and another man from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he wanted to sleep, would rest upon his right side and say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You gather Your servants; he said: So Abu Ishaq said: And the other said: On the Day You resurrect Your servants."
"18665","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was a man of medium build, wide between the shoulders, with abundant hair to the lobes of his ears, upon him a red suit; I never saw anything at all more handsome than him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"18666","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara say: A man recited al-Kahf, and there was an animal in the house, and it began to shy, then he looked and there was a mist or a cloud covering him; they said: So he mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Recite, so-and-so, for it is tranquility that descended at the Quran, or descended for the Quran."
"18667","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara - and a man of Qays asked him, and said: Did you flee from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Hunayn, so al-Bara said: But the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not flee; Hawazin were archers, and when we charged them they scattered, then we fell upon the spoils, and they faced us with arrows; and I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon his white mule, and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith was holding its bridle, and he was saying: I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib."
"18668","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Rabi ibn al-Bara narrate from al-Bara that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he returned from a journey, would say: Returning, repenting, worshipping, to our Lord praising."
"18669","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr informed us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I said to al-Bara: A man charges against the polytheists, is he of those who cast themselves into destruction, he said: No, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: So fight in the way of Allah, you are charged only with yourself; that is only about spending."
"18670","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: It was said to al-Bara: Was the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sharp like this, like the sword, he said: No, rather it was like the moon."
"18671","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and we alighted at Ghadir Khumm, and it was called among us: Prayer in congregation, and a place was swept for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, under two trees, and he prayed Zuhr and took the hand of Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, and said: Do you not know that I am closer to the believers than themselves, they said: Yes, he said: Do you not know that I am closer to every believer than himself, they said: Yes, he said: Then he took the hand of Ali and said: Whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him; he said: Then Umar met him after that and said: Congratulations, O son of Abu Talib, morning and evening you have become the master of every believing man and woman."
"18672","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara ibn Azib from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"18673","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Zubayd informed me - Mansur and Dawud and Ibn Awn and Mujalid from al-Shabi, and this is the hadith of Zubayd - he said: I heard al-Shabi narrate from al-Bara - and he narrated to us at a pillar in the mosque, he said: Had I been there I would have told you its place - he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: The first thing we begin with on this day of ours is to pray, then return and sacrifice; whoever does that has attained our practice; and whoever slaughtered before that, it is only meat he presented to his family, nothing of the rites; he said: And my uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar slaughtered, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered, and I have a young goat better than an old one, he said: Put it in its place, and it will never suffice nor fulfill for anyone after you."
"18674","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Alqamah ibn Marthad said: He informed me from Sad ibn Ubaydah from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about the grave, when he is asked and knows his Lord - he said: And he said something I do not remember - that is the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter."
"18675","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us from al-Bara - Shubah said: And he did not hear it from al-Bara - that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by people of the Ansar and said: If you must do it, spread peace, help the oppressed, and guide the way."
"18676","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a gathering of the Ansar and said: If you insist on sitting, guide the way, return the greeting, and help the oppressed."
"18677","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq that he heard al-Bara say about this verse: Not equal are those who sit among the believers and those who strive in the way of Allah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Zayd, and he brought a shoulder-bone and wrote it; he said: Then Ibn Umm Maktum complained to him of his blindness, and there was revealed: Not equal are those who sit among the believers, other than those with harm."
"18678","Affan narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, he said: A man said to al-Bara, while joking with him: You fled from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, though you are his companions; Al-Bara said: I bear witness concerning the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he did not flee that day; and I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day the trench was dug, carrying soil with the people, reciting the words of Ibn Rawahah: O Allah, were it not for You we would not be guided, nor give charity, nor pray, so send down tranquility upon us, and make feet firm if we meet, for they have transgressed upon us, and if they want tribulation we refuse, prolonging his voice with it."
"18679","Hushaym narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he opened the prayer, raise his hands."
"18680","Hushaym narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Part of the right upon the Muslims is that one of them bathe on Friday, and touch perfume if it is with his family; and if there is no perfume with them, water is most fragrant."
"18681","Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Janab informed us from Yazid ibn al-Bara from his father: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed on the day of sacrifice and said: The first of your rites is this prayer; then Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, my uncle, stood to him - Suhayl said: And he was a Badri - and said: O Messenger of Allah, it was a day in which we desire meat, and we hastened and slaughtered; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Replace it; he said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a young goat; he said: It is for you, and it is for no one after you."
"18682","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abu Janab al-Kalbi narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to me from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We were sitting in the prayer place on the day of sacrifice, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us and greeted the people, then said: The first rite of this day of yours is prayer; he said: So he advanced and prayed two rakahs, then greeted, then faced the people with his face, and he was given a bow or a staff and leaned upon it, and he praised Allah and extolled Him, and commanded them and forbade them, and said: Whoever of you hastened slaughter, it is only a carcass he fed his family; slaughter is only after prayer; so my uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar stood to him and said: I hastened the slaughter of my sheep, O Messenger of Allah, so that food may be made for us which we gather upon when we return, and I have a young she-goat of goats better than what I slaughtered; will it suffice for me, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Yes, and it will never suffice for anyone after you; he said: Then he said: O Bilal; he said: So he walked, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, followed him until he came to the women, and said: O company of women, give charity; charity is better for you; he said: So I never saw a day with more severed bracelets, necklaces and earrings than that day."
"18683","Abu al-Walid and Affan narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you prostrate, place your palms and raise your elbows."
"18684","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Jafar ibn Humayd narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Bara, the like of it."
"18685","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Jafar ibn Humayd narrated it to us, Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Iyad narrated to us from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What do you say of the joy of a man whose mount escapes from him, dragging its rein, in a barren land in which there is no food and no drink, and upon it is food - Affan said: and drink - and he sought it until it became hard upon him, then it passed by the trunk of a tree - Affan said: by a trunk - and its rein caught, and he found it hanging by it - Affan said: attached to it - he said: We said: Severe, O Messenger of Allah; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yet by Allah, Allah is more severe in joy at the repentance of His servant than the man with his mount."
"18686","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Jafar ibn Humayd narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, the like of it."
"18687","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: Not all the hadith we heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; our companions would narrate to us from him; tending camels used to keep us busy from him."
"18688","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from al-Amash from Talhah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Beautify the Quran with your voices."
"18689","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Part of the right upon the Muslims on Friday is to bathe and touch perfume if he finds it; and if he finds no perfume, water is perfume."
"18690","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he first came to Madinah, stayed with his grandfathers and maternal uncles of the Ansar, and he prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen or seventeen months, and he liked that his qiblah be toward the House, and he prayed the first prayer he prayed, the Asr prayer, and a people prayed with him, then a man of those who prayed with him went out and passed by people of a mosque while they were bowing, and said: I bear witness by Allah that I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, toward Makkah; he said: So they turned as they were toward the House; and he liked to be turned toward the House; and the Jews and the People of the Book had been pleased when he prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis, and when he turned his face toward the House they disapproved of that."
"18691","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Jabir from Amir from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed upon his son Ibrahim, and he died at sixteen months, and said: He has in Paradise one to complete his nursing, and he is truthful."
"18692","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: Not all that we narrate to you we heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; but our companions narrated to us, and tending camels used to keep us busy."
"18693","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara or another, he said: A man of the Ansar came with al-Abbas captive, so al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, this one did not capture me; a man of the people captured me, stripped of such-and-such appearance; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to the man: Allah has aided you with a noble angel."
"18694","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Adi ibn Thabit informed me, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None loves the Ansar except a believer, and none hates them except a hypocrite; whoever loves them Allah loves him, and whoever hates them Allah hates him; Shubah said: I said to Adi: Did you hear it from al-Bara, he said: He narrates to me directly."
"18695","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was carrying al-Hasan and said: I love him, so love him."
"18696","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about Ibrahim: A nursing woman in Paradise."
"18697","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Adi ibn Thabit narrated to us from al-Bara that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey, and he recited in the latter Isha, in one of the two rakahs, with: By the fig and the olive."
"18698","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Ashath ibn Sulaym narrated to us from Muawiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us with seven and forbade us seven; he said: So he mentioned what he commanded them of visiting the sick, following funerals, blessing the sneezer, returning the greeting, fulfilling the oath, answering the inviter, and helping the oppressed; and he forbade us silver vessels, and gold rings - or he said: gold circles - and brocade, silk, dibaj, saddle covers, and qassi."
"18699","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from al-Ashath ibn Sulaym, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: blessing the sneezer."
"18700","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me from Qatadah from Abu Ishaq al-Kufi from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah and His angels bless the front row, and the caller to prayer is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and all who hear him, of moist and dry, confirm him, and he has the like of the reward of those who prayed with him."
"18701","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: and Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to me, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it with its isnad."
"18702","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: When this verse was revealed: “Those who stay back among the believers and those who strive in the way of Allah are not equal,” the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Zayd, and he came with a shoulder blade and wrote it. He said: Then Ibn Umm Maktum came and complained of his blindness to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so “other than those who have a disability” was revealed."
"18703","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara say: A man recited Surah al-Kahf, and he had a tied animal, and the animal began to shy. The man looked at a cloud that had covered him, or a mist, and became frightened, and went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) name that man? He said: Yes. He said: “Recite, so-and-so, for tranquility descended for the Qur'an, or at the Qur'an.”"
"18704","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, he said: I heard Ubayd ibn Fayruz, the freedman of Banu Shayban, that he asked al-Bara about the sacrificial animals, what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade and what he disliked. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, or: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us, and my hand is shorter than his hand, and said: “Four do not suffice: the blind whose blindness is clear, the sick whose sickness is clear, the lame whose lameness is clear, and the broken-boned whose marrow is gone.” He said: I said: I dislike that there be a defect in the horn, or he said: a defect in the ear, or a defect in the tooth. He said: “What you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it to anyone.”"
"18705","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating that he heard Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari delivering a sermon, and he said: Al-Bara, and he is not a liar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing, they stood standing until he prostrated, then they prostrated."
"18706","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The first of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to come to us were Mus'ab ibn Umayr and Ibn Umm Maktum. He said: They began teaching the people the Qur'an. Then Ammar and Bilal and Sa'd came. He said: Then Umar ibn al-Khattab came with twenty, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came. I never saw the people of Madinah rejoice at anything at all as they rejoiced at him, until I saw the slave girls and the children saying: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he has come. He said: He did not arrive until I had recited “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” among surahs of the Mufassal."
"18707","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to carry dust with us on the day of al-Ahzab, saying: “O Allah, were it not for You we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed, so send down tranquility upon us. The chiefs have wronged us, and when they want trial we refuse.” Prolonging his voice with it."
"18708","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: al-Hakam narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and his prostration, and what is between the two prostrations, were close to equal."
"18709","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a man of the Ansar to say when he takes his bed: “O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, and laid my back against You, in hope and fear of You. There is no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Prophet whom You sent.” If he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."
"18710","Affan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever grants a grant of silver, or a grant of milk, or guides through a lane, it is like freeing a life.”"
"18711","And whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, it is like freeing a life."
"18712","He said: And he used to come to one side of the row toward its side, straightening their chests and their shoulders, saying: “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.” He said: “Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first rows.”"
"18713","And he used to say: “Beautify the Qur'an with your voices.”"
"18714","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid delivering a sermon: Al-Bara narrated to us, and he was not a liar, that when they prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he raised his head from bowing, they stood standing until they saw him prostrate, then they prostrated."
"18715","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Talhah informed me, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: “Whoever grants a grant of silver, or grants silver, or guides through a lane, or gives milk to drink, it is equal to a neck, or a life.”"
"18716","And whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, ten times, it is like the equal of a neck, or a life."
"18717","He said: And he used to come to us when we stood for prayer and wipe our shoulders or our chests, and he used to say: “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.” And he used to say: “Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row, or the first rows.”"
"18718","Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever calls Madinah Yathrib, let him seek forgiveness from Allah, Mighty and Majestic. It is Tabah, it is Tabah.”"
"18719","Ibn Idris narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut in the morning prayer and in the Maghrib."
"18720","Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah was appointed over prayer in the days of Ibn al-Ash'ath, and when he raised his head from bowing he would stand as long as it takes me to say, and he said: as long as his saying: “O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that, O Possessor of praise and glory. None withholds what You give, and none gives what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail against You.” Al-Hakam said: I narrated that to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, and he said: Al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to me, he said: The bowing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he raised his head from bowing, and his prostration, and what is between the two prostrations, were close to equal."
"18721","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid delivering a sermon, and he said: Al-Bara narrated to us, and he was not a liar, that when they prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he raised his head from bowing, they stood standing until they saw him prostrating, then they prostrated."
"18722","Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions set out. He said: We entered ihram for Hajj. When we arrived at Makkah, he said: “Make your Hajj an Umrah.” He said: The people said: O Messenger of Allah, we entered ihram for Hajj, so how can we make it an Umrah? He said: “Look at what I command you and do it.” They answered him back, so he became angry, then went until he entered upon Aishah angry, and she saw anger in his face and said: Who angered you? May Allah be angry with him. He said: “Why should I not be angry, when I command a matter and am not followed?”"
"18723","Isma'il narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: “Which handhold of Islam is firmest?” They said: Prayer. He said: “Good, but it is not that.” They said: Zakat. He said: “Good, but it is not that.” They said: Fasting Ramadan. He said: “Good, but it is not that.” They said: Hajj. He said: “Good, but it is not that.” They said: Jihad. He said: “Good, but it is not that.” He said: “The firmest handhold of faith is that you love for the sake of Allah and hate for the sake of Allah.”"
"18724","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: A Jew with blackened face and flogged was brought past the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called them and said: “Is this how you find the hadd of the adulterer in your Book?” They said: Yes. He said: Then he called a man of their scholars and said: “I adjure you by Allah who sent down the Torah to Musa, is this how you find the hadd of the adulterer in your Book?” He said: No, by Allah. Were it not that you adjured me by this, I would not have told you. We find the hadd of the adulterer in our Book to be stoning, but it became frequent among our nobles. When we caught a noble we left him, and when we caught a weak one we applied the hadd to him. So we said: Come, let us make something we apply to noble and lowly. So we agreed upon blackening and flogging. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O Allah, I am the first to revive Your command when they killed it.” He said: He ordered him and he was stoned. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “O Messenger, let not those who hasten into disbelief grieve you,” up to His saying: “They say: If you are given this, take it.” They say: Go to Muhammad; if he gives you a ruling of blackening and flogging, take it, and if he gives you a ruling of stoning, beware, up to His saying: “And whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the disbelievers.” He said: Concerning the Jews, up to His saying: “And whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the wrongdoers. And whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the defiantly disobedient.” He said: All of it is concerning the disbelievers."
"18725","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan ibn Thabit: “Lampoon the polytheists, for Jibril is with you.”"
"18726","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that he prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the last Isha, and he recited “By the fig and the olive.”"
"18727","Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Maghrib, and he recited with “By the fig and the olive.”"
"18728","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), His saying: “And whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the disbelievers. And whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the wrongdoers. And whoever does not judge by what Allah sent down, those are the defiantly disobedient.” He said: All of it is concerning the disbelievers."
"18729","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Qanan ibn Abdullah al-Nahmi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Spread peace, you will be safe, and insolence is most evil.”"
"18730","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Qanan ibn Abdullah al-Nahmi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, or grants a grant, or guides through a lane, it is as one who freed a slave.” Abu Abd al-Rahman says: Yahya ibn Adam rarely mentioned people; I never heard him mention anyone except Qanan. He said: He said to us one day, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “This is not of your concern.”"
"18731","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from Mu'awiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded seven and forbade seven. He said: He forbade wearing gold rings, and drinking in silver vessels and gold vessels, and wearing dibaj and silk and istabraq, and wearing qassi, and riding red saddle cloths. And he commanded seven: visiting the sick, following funerals, blessing the sneezer, returning peace, fulfilling the oath, aiding the oppressed, and answering the inviter."
"18732","Isma'il narrated to us: Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of sacrifice and said: “Let no one slaughter until we pray.” My uncle stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is disliked, and I hastened, and I slaughtered my sacrifice to feed my family and the people of my house, or: my family and my neighbors. He said: “You have done it, so repeat with another slaughter.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a young milk goat that is better than two meat sheep; shall I slaughter it? He said: “Yes, and it is the best of your sacrifice, but a jadha'ah will not suffice for anyone after you.”"
"18733","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Minhal ibn Amr, from Zad han, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the funeral of a man of the Ansar, and we reached the grave and it had not yet been given a side niche. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and we sat around him, as if birds were upon our heads, and in his hand was a stick with which he struck the ground. He raised his head and said: “Seek refuge with Allah from the torment of the grave,” two or three times. Then he said: “The believing servant, when he is at the end of this world and the beginning of the Hereafter, angels from heaven descend to him, white-faced, as if their faces are the sun, with them a shroud from the shrouds of Paradise and embalming perfume from the perfume of Paradise, until they sit from him as far as the sight reaches. Then the Angel of Death, peace be upon him, comes until he sits at his head and says: O good soul, come out to forgiveness from Allah and pleasure. He said: It comes out flowing as a drop flows from the mouth of a waterskin. He takes it, and when he takes it they do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye until they take it and place it in that shroud and in that perfume, and there comes from it like the best fragrance of musk found on the face of the earth. He said: They ascend with it and do not pass thereby by any company of angels except they say: What is this good spirit? They say: So-and-so son of so-and-so, by the best of his names by which they called him in this world, until they reach with it the lowest heaven. They ask for it to be opened and it is opened for them. From every heaven its nearest angels escort it to the heaven that follows it, until it is brought to the seventh heaven. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Write the book of My servant in Illiyyun, and return him to the earth, for from it I created them and into it I return them and from it I bring them out another time. He said: His spirit is returned to his body. Two angels come to him and seat him and say to him: Who is your Lord? He says: My Lord is Allah. They say to him: What is your religion? He says: My religion is Islam. They say to him: What is this man who was sent among you? He says: He is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They say to him: What is your knowledge? He says: I read the Book of Allah and believed in it and affirmed it. A caller calls in heaven: My servant has spoken truly, so spread for him from Paradise and clothe him from Paradise and open for him a door to Paradise. He said: There comes to him of its breeze and its fragrance, and his grave is made spacious for him as far as his sight reaches. He said: And there comes to him a man handsome of face, handsome of clothes, sweet of scent, saying: Rejoice in what pleases you; this is your day which you were promised. He says to him: Who are you? Your face is the face that brings good. He says: I am your righteous deed. He says: My Lord, establish the Hour, that I may return to my family and my wealth. He said: And the disbelieving servant, when he is at the end of this world and the beginning of the Hereafter, angels from heaven descend to him, black-faced, with them coarse haircloth. They sit from him as far as the sight reaches. Then the Angel of Death comes until he sits at his head and says: O wicked soul, come out to wrath from Allah and anger. He said: It scatters in his body, and he pulls it as a skewer is pulled from wet wool. He takes it, and when he takes it they do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye until they place it in that haircloth, and there comes from it like the foulest stench of a carcass found on the face of the earth. They ascend with it and do not pass thereby by any company of angels except they say: What is this wicked spirit? They say: So-and-so son of so-and-so, by the ugliest of his names by which he was called in this world, until he is brought to the lowest heaven. Permission is sought for him and it is not opened for him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: “The gates of heaven will not be opened for them, nor will they enter Paradise until the camel passes through the eye of the needle.” Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Write his book in Sijjin, in the lowest earth. His spirit is cast down. Then he recited: “And whoever associates with Allah, it is as if he fell from heaven and the birds snatch him or the wind blows him to a distant place.” His spirit is returned to his body. Two angels come to him and seat him and say to him: Who is your Lord? He says: Hah, hah, I do not know. They say to him: What is your religion? He says: Hah, hah, I do not know. They say to him: What is this man who was sent among you? He says: Hah, hah, I do not know. A caller calls from heaven: He has lied, so spread for him from the Fire and open for him a door to the Fire. There comes to him of its heat and its hot wind, and his grave is narrowed upon him until his ribs differ therein. And there comes to him a man ugly of face, ugly of clothes, foul of scent, saying: Rejoice in what grieves you; this is your day which you were promised. He says: Who are you? Your face is the face that brings evil. He says: I am your wicked deed. He says: My Lord, do not establish the Hour.”"
"18734","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us: al-Minhal ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Umar Zad han, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the funeral of a man of the Ansar, and we reached the grave and it had not yet been given a side niche. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and we sat with him, and he mentioned the like of it. And he said: He pulls it out, with it the veins and nerves are torn. My father said: And likewise said Za'idah."
"18735","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us: Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us: al-Minhal ibn Amr narrated to us: Zad han narrated to us, he said: Al-Bara said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the funeral of a man of the Ansar, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: And there appeared to him a man handsome of clothes, handsome of face, and he said concerning the disbeliever: And there appeared to him a man ugly of face, ugly of clothes."
"18736","Isma'il narrated to us: Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu A'idh Sayf al-Sa'di, and he praised him well, from Yazid ibn al-Bara ibn Azib, and he was a governor in Oman and was as the best of governors, he said: My father said: Gather, and I shall show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution and how he used to pray, for I do not know the extent of my companionship with you. He said: He gathered his sons and his family and called for ablution water. He rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, washed his face three times, washed the right hand three times, washed this hand three times, meaning the left, then wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner, and washed this foot, meaning the right, three times, and washed this foot three times, meaning the left. He said: Thus, I have not spared effort to show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution. Then he entered his house and prayed a prayer we do not know what it is. Then he came out and ordered prayer, and it was established, and he prayed with us the Zuhr, and I think I heard from him verses from Ya-Sin. Then he prayed the Asr, then he prayed with us the Maghrib, then he prayed with us the Isha, and said: I have not spared effort to show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performs ablution and how he used to pray."
"18737","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about ablution from camel meat, and he said: “Perform ablution from it.” He said: And he was asked about prayer in the resting places of camels, and he said: “Do not pray in them, for they are of the devils.” And he was asked about prayer in the resting places of sheep, and he said: “Pray in them, for they are blessing.”"
"18738","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Bara say: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) toward Bayt al-Maqdis sixteen months or seventeen months, Sufyan doubted, then we were turned toward the Ka'bah."
"18739","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, he said: A man said to al-Bara: O Abu Umarah, did you flee on the day of Hunayn? He said: No, by Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not flee, but the hasty people fled. Hawazin met them with arrows. He said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his white mule, and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith holding its bridle, saying: “I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib.”"
"18740","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah: Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Minhal, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam and al-Bara ibn Azib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling gold for silver on credit."
"18741","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Ubayd ibn Fayruz, he said: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib, I said: Narrate to me what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade of sacrificial animals, or what is disliked. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us, and my hand is shorter than his hand, and said: “Four do not suffice: the blind whose blindness is clear, the sick whose sickness is clear, the lame whose lameness is clear, and the broken-boned whose marrow is gone.” I said: I dislike that there be a defect in the tooth, and in the ear a defect, and in the horn a defect. He said: “What you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it to anyone.”"
"18742","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, he said: I heard Ubayd ibn Fayruz, a freedman of Banu Shayban, that he asked al-Bara about sacrificial animals, and he mentioned the hadith."
"18743","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Bara say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a garment of silk, and they began marveling at its beauty and softness. He said: “The handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better, or superior, than this.”"
"18744","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with the people of Makkah on condition that they stay three days, and not enter it except with julubban of weapons. He said: I said: What is julubban of weapons? He said: The quiver and what is in it."
"18745","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from al-Rabi' ibn al-Bara, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from a journey, said: “Returning, repenting, worshipping, to our Lord praising.”"
"18746","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “No two Muslims meet and shake hands except they are forgiven before they part.”"
"18747","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Abu Dawud, he said: I met al-Bara ibn Azib, and he greeted me and took my hand and laughed in my face. He said: Do you know why I did this with you? He said: I said: No, I do not know, but I do not see you did it except for good. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me and did with me the like of what I did with you. He asked me, and I said the like of what you said to me. He said: “No two Muslims meet, and one greets his companion and takes his hand, taking it only for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, but they do not part until they are forgiven.”"
"18748","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Ajlah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: “You will meet the enemy tomorrow, and your war cry is Ha-Mim; they will not be aided.”"
"18749","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-A'mash informed us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: al-A'mash, I think, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died when sixteen months old. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to be buried in al-Baqi', and said: “He has a nursing mother who nurses him in Paradise.”"
"18750","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi narrating, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning his son Ibrahim: “He has a nursing mother who nurses him in Paradise.”"
"18751","Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he slept, placed his hand upon his cheek, then said: “O Allah, protect me from Your torment on the day You resurrect Your servants.”"
"18752","Waki' narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from Yazid ibn al-Bara ibn Azib, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of what we loved, or of what he loves, is that he stand on his right. He said: And I heard him say: “My Lord, protect me from Your torment on the day You resurrect Your servants,” or: “gather Your servants.”"
"18753","Abu Nu'aym narrated it to us with its isnad and its meaning, except that he said: Thabit, from Ibn al-Bara, from al-Bara."
"18754","Waki' narrated to us: my father and Sufyan and Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We used to say that the number of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr was as the number of the companions of Talut on the day of Jalut, three hundred and a dozen-odd, those who crossed the river with him. He said: None crossed the river with him except a believer."
"18755","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: “Those who stay back among the believers, other than those who have a disability.” He said: When it was revealed, Amr ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was blind of sight. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me? I am blind of sight. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “Other than those who have a disability.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Bring me the shoulder blade and the ink, or the tablet and the ink.”"
"18756","Waki' narrated to us: Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, he said: I met my uncle with him the banner. I said: Where are you going? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him, to strike his neck, or: to kill him, and take his property."
"18757","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I never saw one with long hair more handsome in a red suit than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He had hair reaching his shoulders, wide between the shoulders, neither short nor tall."
"18758","Waki' narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaigned in fifteen expeditions."
"18759","Waki' narrated to us: Fitr narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaigned in fifteen expeditions."
"18760","Waki' narrated to us: Fitr narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: “When you go to your bed in a state of purity, say: O Allah, I have submitted my face to You, laid my back against You, entrusted my affair to You, in hope and fear of You. There is no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Prophet whom You sent. If you die in your night, you die upon the fitrah, and if you wake, you wake having attained much good.” Fitr heard it from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah."
"18761","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned."
"18762","Waki' narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: We reached al-Hudaybiyah, and it is a well that had been drained, and we were fourteen hundred. He said: A bucket was drawn from it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rinsed his mouth from it, then spat into it, and supplicated. He said: We drank and watered. Waki' said: Fourteen hundred."
"18763","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), fourteen hundred, at al-Hudaybiyah, and al-Hudaybiyah is a well. We drained it and left nothing in it. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came and sat on its edge and called for a vessel. He rinsed his mouth, then spat into it. Then we left it a short while, and it poured forth for us, we and our mounts, drinking from it as we wished."
"18764","Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara say: A man of the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covered in iron and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I submit or fight? He said: “No, rather submit, then fight.” He submitted, then fought, and was killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “He did little and was rewarded much.”"
"18765","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Mis'ar informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in the Isha prayer with “By the fig and the olive.” He said: And I never heard a man with better recitation than him."
"18766","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with the people of al-Hudaybiyah, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote a document between them. He said: He wrote: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. The polytheists said: Do not write: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. Had you been the Messenger of Allah we would not have fought you. He said: He said to Ali: “Erase it.” He said: He said: I am not one to erase it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) erased it with his hand. He said: And he made peace with them on condition that he and his companions enter three days, and not enter it except with julubban of weapons. I asked: What is julubban of weapons? He said: The quiver with what is in it."
"18767","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara say: The first of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to arrive at Madinah were Mus'ab ibn Umayr and Ibn Umm Maktum, and they used to teach the people. He said: Then Bilal and Sa'd and Ammar ibn Yasir arrived. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, arrived with twenty of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived. I never saw the people of Madinah rejoice at anything as they rejoiced at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The slave girls began saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has arrived. He said: He did not arrive until I had recited “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” among surahs of the Mufassal."
"18768","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Affan narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: Affan said: Abu Ishaq informed us, from al-Bara, and Abu Ishaq did not hear it from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people sitting in the road and said: “If you must do it, guide the way, return peace, and aid the oppressed.” Affan said: And help. My father said: Abu Sa'id narrated it to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq say: Help the oppressed. My father said:"
"18769","And Aswad narrated it to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Bara, and he said: Help the oppressed. And likewise said Hasan: Help, and from Isra'il."
"18770","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Ahzab used to carry dust with us, and the dust had covered the whiteness of his belly, saying: “O Allah, were it not for You we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed, so send down tranquility upon us. The chiefs have wronged us.” And perhaps he said: “The assembly has wronged us. When they want trial we refuse.” Raising his voice with it."
"18771","Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, and from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Trench carrying dust, and he mentioned the like of it."
"18772","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Bara, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Trench carrying dust, and he mentioned the like of it."
"18773","Muhammad and Hashim narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: On the day of Khaybar we got donkeys. The crier of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: “Overturn the pots.”"
"18774","Hashim narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"18775","And Ibn Ja'far in this hadith said: I heard al-Bara and Ibn Abi Awfa."
"18776","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He mentioned the torment of the grave. He said: It is said to him: Who is your Lord? He says: Allah is my Lord, and my Prophet is Muhammad. That is His saying: “Allah keeps firm those who believe, with the firm word in the life of this world,” meaning thereby the Muslim."
"18777","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib narrating that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning the Ansar: “None loves them except a believer, and none hates them except a hypocrite. Whoever loves them, Allah loves him, and whoever hates them, Allah hates him.” He said: I said to him: Did you hear al-Bara? He said: He narrates to me directly."
"18778","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, upon his shoulder, saying: “O Allah, I love him, so love him.”"
"18779","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', he said: I heard Adi ibn Thabit narrating from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: People passed by us going out. We said: Where are you going? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us to a man who took his father's wife, to kill him."
"18780","Hushaym narrated to us: Ash'ath informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: My uncle al-Harith ibn Amr passed by me, with him a banner the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had tied for him. I said to him: O uncle, where has the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent you? He said: He sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and commanded me to strike his neck."
"18781","Hushaym narrated to us: al-Hajjaj informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: Among what the people of Makkah stipulated upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that none of his companions enter it with a weapon, except a weapon in a quiver."
"18782","Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Awwam, from Azrah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we stood in rows until, when he prostrated, we followed him."
"18783","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, he said: I heard al-Bara narrating to people among whom was Ka'b ibn Ujrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to the Ansar: “You will meet after me selfish preference. They said: What do you command us? He said: Be patient until you meet me at the Basin.”"
"18784","Hashim narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abu Busrah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eighteen journeys, and never saw him leave the two rak'ahs before Zuhr."
"18785","Hashim narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd, from Yunus, from al-Bara, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a march, and we came to a well with little water, meaning scanty water. He said: Six descended into it, I being the sixth, drawing water. A bucket was let down to us. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the edge of the well. We put in it half of it, or about two-thirds of it, and it was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Bara said: I almost, with my vessel, sought something to put in my throat, and found nothing. The bucket was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He dipped his hand in it and said what Allah willed him to say. The bucket was returned to us with what was in it. He said: I saw one of us taken out by his garment for fear of drowning. He said: Then it flowed, meaning it ran as a river."
"18786","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: And Hudbah narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Yunus, from al-Bara, the like of it. He said therein also: drawing water."
"18787","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: We campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fifteen expeditions, and I and Abdullah ibn Umar are of the same age."
"18788","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Fudayl, meaning Ibn Iyad, narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: “When you go to your bed, perform ablution and sleep on your right side and say: O Allah, I have submitted my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, and laid my back against You, in fear and hope of You. There is no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down and in Your Prophet whom You sent. If you die, you die upon the fitrah.”"
"18789","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Mubarak informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, and he mentioned with its isnad and its meaning. And he said: Perform ablution as your ablution for prayer. And he said: Make them the last of what you speak. He said: I repeated it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When I reached: I believe in Your Book which You sent down, I said: And in Your Messenger. He said: No, and in Your Prophet whom You sent."
"18790","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about kalalah. He said: “The summer verse suffices you.”"
"18791","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a gathering of the Ansar and said: “If you refuse but to sit, guide the way, return peace, and help the oppressed.”"
"18792","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: A man used to recite Surah al-Kahf in his house, and beside him his horse tied with two ropes, until a cloud covered him and began drawing near and near, until his horse began to shy from it. The man said: I marveled at that. In the morning he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him and told him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “That is tranquility descending for the Qur'an.”"
"18793","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covered in iron and said: Shall I fight or submit? He said: “Rather submit, then fight.” He submitted, then fought, and was killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “He did little and was rewarded much.”"
"18794","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us that al-Bara ibn Azib said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed Abdullah ibn Jubayr over the archers on the day of Uhud, and they were fifty men. He said: He positioned them and said: “If you see us snatched by birds, do not leave until I send to you. And if you see us prevail over the enemy and trample them, do not leave until I send to you.” He said: They routed them. He said: By Allah, I saw the women running on the mountain, their shins and anklets visible, raising their garments. The companions of Abdullah ibn Jubayr said: Booty, O people, booty! Your companions have prevailed; what are you waiting for? Abdullah ibn Jubayr said: Did you forget what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to you? They said: By Allah, we shall go to the people and take from the booty. When they went to them, their faces were turned back, and they came retreating. That is what the Messenger calls them in their rear. None remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except twelve men. They struck from us seventy men. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions had struck of the polytheists on the day of Badr one hundred forty: seventy captives and seventy killed. Abu Sufyan said: Is Muhammad among the people? Is Muhammad among the people? Is Muhammad among the people? Three times. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to answer him. Then he said: Is the son of Abu Quhafah among the people? Is the son of Abu Quhafah among the people? Is the son of al-Khattab among the people? Is the son of al-Khattab among the people? Then he turned to his companions and said: As for these, they have been killed, and you are spared them. Umar could not control himself and said: You lied, O enemy of Allah. Those you named are all alive, and there remains for you what will grieve you. He said: A day for the day of Badr, and war is seesaw. You will find among the people mutilation I did not command and it did not displease me. Then he began chanting: Rise, Hubal, rise, Hubal. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Will you not answer him?” They said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we say? He said: “Say: Allah is Highest and Most Majestic.” He said: We have al-Uzza and you have no Uzza. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Will you not answer him?” They said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we say? He said: “Say: Allah is our Protector and you have no protector.”"
"18795","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Balj Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hakam Ali al-Basri narrated to us, from Abu Bahr, from al-Bara, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “No two Muslims meet and one takes the hand of his companion, then praises Allah, but they part with no sin between them.”"
"18796","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Isra'il informed us, or another, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, he said: A garment of silk was given to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We began touching it and marveling at it, saying: We never saw a garment better than it and softer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Does this please you?” We said: Yes. He said: “The handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this and softer.”"
"18797","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Qutaybah wrote it to me: Abthr ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Burd, brother of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever follows a funeral until he prays over it, he has of reward a qirat. And whoever walks with the funeral until it is buried, and once he said: until he is buried, he has of reward two qirats. And the qirat is like Uhud.”"
"18798","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Salih ibn Abdullah al-Tirmidhi and Abu Ma'mar narrated it to us, they said: Abthr ibn al-Qasim Abu Zubayd narrated to us, from Burd, brother of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from al-Bara, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"18799","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Humayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I observed the prayer with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found his standing, his bowing, his straightening after bowing, his prostration, his sitting between the two prostrations, his sitting between the taslim, and what is between the taslim and leaving, close to equal."
"18800","Affan narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us: Iyad narrated to us, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When you prostrate, place your palms and raise your elbows.”"
"18801","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Zuhayr from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed Abdullah ibn Jubayr over the archers, and they were fifty men, on the day of Uhud, and said: If you see the enemy, and you see the birds snatching us away, do not leave your place. Then when they saw the spoils, they said: To the spoils. Abdullah said: Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not leave. Another narrator said: So they came down, and there was revealed: and you disobeyed after He had shown you what you love — meaning: you disobeyed the Messenger after He had shown you the spoils and the rout of the enemy."
"18802","Narrated to us Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri and Husayn ibn Muhammad, in meaning, they said: Narrated to us Abu Raja Abdullah ibn Waqid al-Harawi, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Malik from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he caught sight of a group of people, so he said: What have these gathered for. It was said: Over a grave they are digging. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was startled and hastened ahead of his Companions until he reached the grave, then he knelt upon it. He said: So I faced him from in front of him in order to see what he does, and he wept until he wetted the soil with his tears, then he turned to us and said: O my brothers, prepare for a day like this."
"18803","Narrated to us Abu Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us Abu Raja, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Malik, he said: I saw upon al-Bara a ring of gold, and the people were saying to him: Why do you wear gold as a ring when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it. So al-Bara said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and before him was spoils he was distributing, captives and khurthi, he said: So he distributed it until this ring remained, then he raised his glance and looked at his Companions, then lowered it, then raised his glance and looked at them, then lowered it, then raised his glance and looked at them, then said: O Bara. So I came to him until I sat before him, then he took the ring and seized my wrist, then said: Take, wear what Allah and His Messenger have clothed you with. He said: And al-Bara used to say: How do you command me to put down what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about: Wear what Allah and His Messenger have clothed you with."
"18804","Narrated to us Hajjaj, Shu'ba informed us from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar, he said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa narrating from al-Bara that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he woke up, would say: Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection. Shu'ba said: This or something like this in meaning. And when he slept, he would say: O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die."
"18805","Narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Hubab, narrated to us al-Husayn, meaning Ibn Waqid, narrated to us Abu Ishaq, al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prostrate upon the fleshy parts of the palms."
"18806","Narrated to us Yunus ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Fulayh from Safwan ibn Sulaym from Abu Busrata from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some ten campaigns, and I never saw him leave the two rak'as when the sun declines."
"18807","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, narrated to us al-Awza'i from al-Zuhri from Haram ibn Muhayyisa from al-Bara ibn Azib that he had a vicious she-camel, and it entered a walled garden and caused damage in it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that guarding of walled gardens by day is upon their owners, and that guarding of livestock by night is upon their owners, and that whatever livestock destroy by night is guaranteed by their owners."
"18808","Narrated to us Ma'mar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi, narrated to us al-Hajjaj from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about kalala, so he said: The summer verse suffices you."
"18809","Narrated to us Asbat, he said: Narrated to us Mutarrif from Abu al-Jahm from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I was going around lost camels of mine in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was roaming among dwellings, when I came upon a riding party with horsemen, and they came and circled my courtyard, then they brought out a man, and they did not ask him nor speak to him until they struck his neck. Then when they left, I asked about him, and they said: He married the wife of his father."
"18810","Narrated to us Aswad ibn Amir, narrated to us Abu Bakr from Mutarrif, he said: They came to a dome and brought out a man from it and killed him. He said: I said: What is this. They said: This is a man who married his wife's mother, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to him, and they killed him."
"18811","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, narrated to us Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim, Adi ibn Thabit narrated to me, he said: Yazid ibn al-Bara narrated to me from his father, he said: I met my maternal uncle with a banner with him, so I said: Where are you going. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us to a man of Banu Tamim who married his father's wife after him, and he commanded us to kill him and take his wealth. He said: So they did. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father did not narrate from Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar except this hadith, because of his defect."
"18812","Narrated to us Aswad ibn Amir and Abu Ahmad, they said: Narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man was fasting and the time of breaking fast came but he slept before breaking fast, would not eat that night nor that day until evening. And a certain Ansari man was fasting, and when the breaking of fast came to him, he came to his wife and said: Do you have any food. She said: No, but I will go and seek some for you. Then his eyes overcame him, and his wife came, and when she saw him she said: Disappointment for you. So he woke in the morning, and when midday came he fainted, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so this verse was revealed: Permitted to you on the night of fasting is intimacy with your wives, up to His saying: until the white thread becomes clear to you from the black thread. Abu Ahmad said: And Qays ibn Sirma al-Ansari came and slept, then he mentioned him."
"18813","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, he said: Narrated to us Zuhayr, narrated to us Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib that one of them, when he slept, then he mentioned something like the hadith of Isra'il, except that he said: It was revealed concerning Abu Qays ibn Amr."
"18814","Narrated to us Aswad ibn Amir, Isra'il informed us, narrated to us Abu Ishaq, and narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: I never saw anyone of Allah's creation more handsome in a red suit than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his hair indeed reaches to his shoulders. Ibn Abi Bukayr said: Striking close to his shoulders. And I heard him narrating it many times; he never narrated it except that he laughed."
"18815","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Ma'mar from Yunus ibn Khabbab from al-Minhal ibn Amr from Zadham from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to a funeral, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the grave and we sat around him as if birds were upon our heads, while a niche was being dug for him. So he said: I seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, three times. Then he said: Indeed the believer, when he is approaching the Hereafter and departing from this world, angels descend to him as if their faces were the sun, with each one a shroud and embalming perfume, and they sit from him as far as the eye can see, until when his soul comes out, every angel between heaven and earth prays upon him, and every angel in heaven, and the gates of heaven are opened for him; there is no people of a gate except that they call upon Allah that his soul be taken up from their side. Then when his soul is taken up, they say: Lord, Your servant so-and-so. So He says: Return him, for I covenanted to them that from it I created them, and into it I shall return them, and from it I shall bring them out another time. He said: So he hears the striking of his companions' sandals when they turn away from him, then a comer comes to him and says: Who is your Lord, what is your religion, who is your prophet. So he says: My Lord is Allah, and my religion is Islam, and my prophet is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he rebukes him and says: Who is your Lord, what is your religion, who is your prophet, and it is the last trial presented to the believer, and that is when Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. So he says: My Lord is Allah, and my religion is Islam, and my prophet is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he says to him: You spoke the truth. Then a comer comes to him, handsome of face, sweet of scent, fine of clothes, and says: Rejoice in honor from Allah and abiding bliss. So he says: And you, may Allah give you glad tidings of good, who are you. So he says: I am your righteous deed. By Allah, you were quick in obedience to Allah, slow toward disobedience to Allah, so may Allah reward you with good. Then a gate of Paradise and a gate of Hell are opened for him, and it is said: This would have been your abode had you disobeyed Allah; Allah has replaced it for you with this. Then when he sees what is in Paradise, he says: Lord, hasten the Hour so that I may return to my family and wealth. So it is said to him: Reside. And indeed the disbeliever, when he is departing from this world and approaching the Hereafter, stern harsh angels descend upon him, and they wrench out his soul as a many-pronged skewer is wrenched from wet wool, and his soul is pulled out along with the veins, and every angel between heaven and earth curses him, and every angel in heaven, and the gates of heaven are closed; there is no people of a gate except that they call upon Allah that his soul not be taken up from their side. Then when his soul is taken up, they say: Lord, so-and-so son of so-and-so, Your servant. He says: Return him, for I covenanted to them that from it I created them, and into it I shall return them, and from it I shall bring them out another time. He said: So he hears the striking of his companions' sandals when they turn away from him. He said: Then a comer comes to him and says: Who is your Lord, what is your religion, who is your prophet. So he says: I do not know. So he says: You did not know and you did not recite. And a comer comes to him, ugly of face, ugly of clothes, foul of scent, and says: Rejoice in humiliation from Allah and abiding punishment. So he says: And you, may Allah give you glad tidings of evil, who are you. So he says: I am your evil deed. You were slow toward obedience to Allah, quick in disobedience to Allah, so may Allah reward you with evil. Then a blind deaf mute one is set over him, in his hand a mallet; if a mountain were struck with it, it would become dust. So he strikes him a blow until he becomes dust, then Allah restores him as he was, then he strikes him another blow, and he cries out a cry heard by everything except the two weighty beings. Al-Bara ibn Azib said: Then a gate of Hell is opened for him, and bedding of Hell is spread, and"
"18816","Abu al-Rabi narrated it to us, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd from Yunus ibn Khabbab from al-Minhal ibn Amr from Zadham from al-Bara ibn Azib, the like of it."
"18817","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, Sufyan informed us from Mansur and al-A'mash from Talha from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja al-Nahmi from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah and His angels bless the first rows."
"18818","And beautify the Quran with your voices."
"18819","And whoever grants a milch-animal as a loan, or a loan of silver, or guides to a lane, then it is like freeing a neck."
"18820","Narrated to us Ali ibn Asim, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us from Sa'd ibn Ubayda from al-Bara ibn Azib from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man lies down and pillows his right side, then says: O Allah, to You I submit myself, and to You I entrust my affair, and to You I lean my back, and to You I turn my face, in fear of You and desire for You. There is no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and in Your Prophet whom You sent; and he dies upon that, a house is built for him in Paradise, or a house is prepared for him in Paradise."
"18821","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba, he said: Narrated to us Abu Khalid al-Ahmar from al-Hasan ibn Amr from Talha from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows; let there not come between you like the offspring of hadhaf. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the offspring of hadhaf. He said: Black hairless ones that are in the land of Yemen."
"18822","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba, he said: Narrated to us Sharik from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes to the open country becomes harsh."
"18823","Narrated to us Uthman ibn Muhammad, he said: Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Uthman, he said: Narrated to us Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid from Mutarrif from Abu al-Jahm from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a man who married his father's wife, that he be killed."
"18824","Narrated to us Harun ibn Ma'ruf, he said: Abdullah said: And I think I heard it from him, he said: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja narrated to me from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us and wipe our shoulders and chests, and say: Let your rows not differ, lest your hearts differ. Indeed Allah and His angels bless the first row, or the first rows."
"18825","Narrated to us Affan, narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Mughira, narrated to us Humayd ibn Hilal, narrated to us Yunus from al-Bara, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we came to a well with little water. Six went down into it, I being their seventh, or seven, I being their eighth. He said: A bucket was let down to us, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the edge of the well. So I put into it half of it, or nearly a third of it, then the bucket was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Bara said: And I almost, with my vessel, sought something to put in my throat, but I found nothing. So he dipped his hand into it, and said what Allah willed him to say, and the bucket was returned to us with what was in it, and the last of us was brought out with a garment, fearing drowning. Then it flowed. And Affan once said: Fearing drowning."
"18826","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Ma'mar from Asim from al-Sha'bi from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us on the day of Khaybar from the flesh of domestic donkeys, cooked and raw."
"18827","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Abu al-Duha from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died at sixteen months, so he said: Bury him in al-Baqi, for he has a nursing mother who will complete his suckling in Paradise."
"18828","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Sufyan from al-A'mash from al-Minhal from Zadham from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a funeral, and we found the grave not yet given a niche, so he sat and we sat."
"18829","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Ma'mar from Ash'ath from Adi ibn Thabit from Yazid ibn al-Bara from his father, he said: My uncle met me with a banner with him, so I said: Where are you going. So he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and commanded me to kill him."
"18830","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Zakariyya, narrated to us Abu Ya'qub al-Thaqafi, Yunus ibn Ubayd, the freedman of Muhammad ibn al-Qasim, narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim sent me to al-Bara ibn Azib to ask him about the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what it was. He said: It was black, square, made of namira."
"18831","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas from Mansur from al-Sha'bi from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of sacrifice after the prayer."
"18832","Narrated to us Yazid, he said: Zakariyya informed us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umra before he performed Hajj, and he performed Umra before he performed Hajj. Then Aisha said: He knew that he performed four Umras, including his Umra in which he performed Hajj."
"18833","Narrated to us Yazid, Dawud informed us, and Ibn Abi Adi from Dawud, in meaning, from Amir from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — Ibn Abi Adi said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: Let no one slaughter before we pray. Then my maternal uncle stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is abundant — Ibn Abi Adi said: Disliked — and I have slaughtered my sacrifice beforehand so that my family and neighbors may eat, and I have a milch kid better than two meat sheep, shall I slaughter it. He said: Yes, but a jadha'a will not suffice for anyone after you, and it is the better of your two sacrifices."
"18834","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to sleep, would place his cheek upon his right hand and say: Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants."
"18835","Narrated to us Yazid, Shu'ba informed us from Abu Ishaq from al-Rabi ibn al-Bara from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he returned from a journey, he would say: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord."
"18836","Narrated to us Yazid, Shu'ba informed us, Sharik ibn Abdullah informed us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deemed me and Ibn Umar young, so we were sent back on the day of Badr."
"18837","Narrated to us Abda ibn Sulayman al-Kilabi, narrated to us Mis'ar from al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from al-Bara, he said: The bowing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his standing after bowing, and his sitting between the two prostrations — we do not know which of them is longest."
"18838","Narrated to us Hujayn, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umra in Dhu al-Qa'da, but the people of Mecca refused to let him enter Mecca until they made terms with him to stay in it three days. Then when they wrote the document, they wrote: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has agreed upon. They said: We do not affirm this; had we known that you are the Messenger of Allah, we would not have barred you from anything. Rather, you are Muhammad ibn Abdullah. He said: I am the Messenger of Allah, and I am Muhammad ibn Abdullah. He said to Ali: Erase Messenger of Allah. He said: By Allah, I will never erase you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the document, though he was not good at writing, and wrote in place of Messenger of Allah: This is what Muhammad ibn Abdullah has agreed upon: that he not bring weapons into Mecca except the sword in its sheath, and that none of its people leave except whoever wishes to follow him, and that he not prevent any of his Companions from staying in it. Then when he entered it and the term elapsed, they came to Ali and said: Tell your companion to leave us, for the term has elapsed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left."
"18839","And Aswad ibn Amir narrated it to us, Isra'il informed us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umra in Dhu al-Qa'da, then he mentioned its meaning, and said: That he not bring weapons into Mecca, and that none of its people leave."
"18840","Narrated to us Hujayn, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: While a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and a horse of his, a stallion, was tied in the house, it began to shy. So the man went out and looked but saw nothing, and it kept shying. Then in the morning he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: That was tranquility descending with the Quran."
"18841","Narrated to us Hujayn, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The last sura revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complete was Bara'a, and the last verse revealed was the seal of Surat al-Nisa: They ask you for a ruling, to the end of the sura."
"18842","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Mis'ar from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in the Isha prayer: By the fig and the olive. And I never heard a better voice nor a better prayer than his."
"18843","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam and Husayn, they said: Narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah and His angels bless the foremost row."
"18844","Narrated to us Yahya and Husayn, they said: Narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umra in Dhu al-Qa'da."
"18845","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan ibn Thabit: Lampoon the polytheists, for the Holy Spirit is with you."
"18846","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Ammar ibn Ruzayq from Abu Ishaq from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja from al-Bara ibn Azib, testifying it upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah and His angels bless the first rows."
"18847","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Sufyan from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha from Mu'awiya ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us with seven and forbade us seven. He commanded us to visit the sick, and to follow funeral processions, and to answer the inviter, and to spread greeting, and to bless the sneezer, and to fulfill the oath, and to aid the oppressed. And he forbade us gold rings, and silver vessels, and silk, and dibaj, and istabraq, and red saddle cloths, and qassi."
"18848","Narrated to us Abu Dawud Umar ibn Sa'd from Sufyan the like of it, but he did not mention in it the spreading of greeting, and he said: He forbade us gold and silver vessels."
"18849","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and Ammar ibn Ruzayq from Abu Ishaq from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah and His angels bless the first rows."
"18850","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam and Abu Ahmad, they said: Narrated to us Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Bajali, of Banu Bajala, of Banu Sulaym, from Talha — Abu Ahmad said: Narrated to us Talha ibn Musarrif — from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed that will admit me to Paradise. So he said: Though you shortened the address, you have posed a broad question. Free the person, and ransom the neck. He said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not one. He said: No. Freeing the person is that you alone free it, and ransoming the neck is that you help in freeing it. And the rich milch gift, and kindness to the unjust kinsman. Then if you cannot do that, feed the hungry, and give drink to the thirsty, and command good and forbid evil. Then if you cannot do that, withhold your tongue except from good."
"18851","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Sufyan from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib saying: When this verse was revealed: And Allah favored the strivers over those who sit with a great reward, Ibn Umm Maktum came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me, for I am blind of sight. He said: So there was revealed: Except those with harm. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the shoulder blade and the ink, or the tablet and the ink."
"18852","Narrated to us Waki from his father and Ali ibn Salih from Ash'ath ibn Sulaym from Mu'awiya ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin — my father said, and Abd al-Rahman said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, he said: I heard Mu'awiya ibn Suwayd from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us with seven and forbade us seven. He commanded us to visit the sick, and to follow funeral processions, and to bless the sneezer, and to return greeting, and to answer the inviter, and to aid the oppressed, and to fulfill the swearer. And he forbade us gold and silver vessels, and wearing gold as a ring, and wearing silk, and dibaj, and qassi, and red saddle cloths, and istabraq. And Abd al-Rahman did not mention gold and silver vessels."
"18853","Narrated to us Waki from Shu'ba from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan: Attack them, or lampoon them, for Jibril is with you."
"18854","Narrated to us Waki from Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: When you go to your bed, say: O Allah, I submit my face to You, and I lean my back to You, and I entrust my affair to You, in desire and fear of You. There is no refuge nor escape except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and in Your Prophet whom You sent. Then if you die, you die upon the fitra, and if you wake, you wake having attained good."
"18855","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us Sufyan, he said: I heard Amr ibn Murra, or he said: He narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from al-Bara that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate qunut in the dawn and sunset prayers. Shu'ba said the like of it."
"18856","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman from Shu'ba from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: And Ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us from Abu Ishaq that he heard al-Bara, he said: When there was revealed: Not equal are those who sit among the believers and the strivers in the way of Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Zayd, so he came with a shoulder blade and wrote it. Then Ibn Umm Maktum complained of his blindness, so there was revealed: Not equal are those who sit among the believers, except those with harm."
"18857","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Ja'far, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined a man, when he takes his bed, to say: O Allah, I submit myself to You, and I turn my face to You, and I entrust my affair to You, and I lean my back to You, in desire and fear of You. There is no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and in Your Prophet whom You sent. Then if he dies, he dies upon the fitra."
"18858","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Ja'far, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Amr ibn Murra from Sa'd ibn Ubayda from al-Bara from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of that."
"18859","Ibn Ja'far said: Shu'ba said: And he informed me from al-Hasan from al-Bara ibn Azib with the like of that."
"18860","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Yazid, he said: Al-Bara narrated to us, and he is not a liar, he said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he raised his head from bowing, no man of us would bend his back until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, then we would prostrate."
"18861","He said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came from a journey, would say: Returning, repenting, praising our Lord."
"18862","Narrated to us Abd al-Malik ibn Amr from Shu'ba from Abu Ishaq from al-Rabi ibn al-Bara from his father al-Bara ibn Azib the like of that."
"18863","Narrated to us Aswad ibn Amir, Isra'il informed us from Abu Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he slept, would place his right hand under his cheek and say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants."
"18864","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Shu'ba and Sufyan from Amr ibn Murra from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ibn Azib that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated qunut in the dawn prayer."
"18865","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Trench carrying soil, and the soil had covered the hair of his chest."
"18866","Narrated to us Waki, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Murra from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jew, and said: O Allah, I bear witness that I am the first who revived a sunna they had killed."
"18867","Narrated to us Waki, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has a nursing mother in Paradise."
"18868","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us al-A'mash from Talha ibn Musarrif from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants a loan of silver, or a loan of milk, or guides to a lane, it is for him like the equivalent of a neck. And he once said: Like freeing a neck."
"18869","Narrated to us Waki from Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: I never saw one with flowing hair more handsome in a red suit than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He had hair striking his shoulders, wide between the shoulders, neither tall nor short."
"18870","Narrated to us Waki and Ibn Ja'far, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ubayd ibn Firuz, the freedman of Banu Shayban, in his hadith, he said: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked of sacrifices, or what he forbade of sacrifices. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us — he said: And his hand is longer than my hand, or he said: My hand is shorter than his hand — he said: Four do not avail in sacrifices: the blind whose blindness is evident, and the sick whose sickness is evident, and the lame whose lameness is evident, and the broken whose marrow is gone. So I said to al-Bara: We dislike that there be a defect in the ear, or a defect in the eye, or a defect in the tooth. He said: Whatever you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it to anyone."
"18871","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a garment of silk, and his Companions began to marvel at its softness. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are softer than this."
"18872","Narrated to us Waki from his father from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaigned fifteen campaigns."
"18873","Narrated to us Waki from Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us on the day of Khaybar while we had cooked the pots, so he said: What is this. We said: Donkeys we seized. He said: Wild or domestic. We said: Domestic. He said: Overturn them."
"18874","Narrated to us Waki, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Hudaybiyya, and al-Hudaybiyya is a well. He said: And we were fourteen hundred. He said: And there was little water in it. He said: So he pulled a bucket, then rinsed, then spat, and supplicated. He said: So we drank our fill and watered."
"18875","Narrated to us Waki from Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Yazid from al-Bara that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, would place his right hand under his cheek and say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants, or gather Your servants."
"18876","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Fudayl, meaning Ibn Marzuq, from Shaqiq ibn Uqba from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: There was revealed: Guard the prayers and the Asr prayer. So we recited it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as long as Allah willed us to recite it; Allah did not abrogate it. Then He sent down: Guard the prayers and the middle prayer. Then a man with Shaqiq called Azhar said to him: And it is the Asr prayer. He said: I already told you how it came down and how Allah the Exalted abrogated it, and Allah knows best."
"18877","Narrated to us Asbat, narrated to us Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer, would raise his hands until his thumbs were level with his ears."
"18878","Narrated to us Uthman ibn Umar, he said: Malik, meaning Ibn Abi Anas, narrated to us from Amr ibn al-Harith from Ubayd ibn Firuz from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked what is avoided of sacrifices. So he said: Four. And al-Bara said: And my hand is shorter than the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the lame whose limping is evident, and the blind whose blindness is evident, and the sick whose sickness is evident, and the emaciated that has no marrow."
"18879","Narrated to us Abu Sa'id, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people of the Ansar in their gatherings and said: If you must do so, guide the way, and return greeting, and aid the oppressed."
"18880","And Muhammad ibn Ja'far said from Shu'ba: Abu Ishaq said from al-Bara, but Abu Ishaq did not hear it from al-Bara."
"18881","Narrated to us Ma'mar, narrated to us al-Hajjaj from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about kalala, so he said: The summer verse suffices you."
"18882","Narrated to us Husayn, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Hassan, lampoon the polytheists, for Jibril is with you, or indeed the Holy Spirit is with you, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"18883","Narrated to us Hashim ibn al-Qasim, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Call Zayd to me; let him come, or bring, with the shoulder blade and the ink, or the tablet and the ink. He wrote: Not equal are those who sit among the believers and the strivers in the way of Allah. He said: Thus it came down. He said: Then Ibn Umm Maktum, behind his back, said: O Messenger of Allah, my eyes are impaired. He said: So there was revealed, before he moved: Except those with harm."
"18884","Narrated to us Ali ibn Hafs, narrated to us Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you go to your bed, say: O Allah, I submit myself to You, and I turn my face to You, and I entrust my affair to You, and I lean my back to You, in desire and fear of You. There is no refuge nor escape except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and in Your Prophet whom You sent. Then if you die that night, you die upon the fitra, and if you wake, you attain good."
"18885","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah Abu Ahmad, and Mis'ar narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from al-Bara, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the Isha prayer: By the fig and the olive. And I never heard anyone with a better voice than his when he recited, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"18886","Narrated to us Asbat ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer, would raise his hands until his thumbs were level with his ears."
"18887","Narrated to us Mu'ammal, narrated to us Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made truce with the polytheists on the day of al-Hudaybiyya upon three things: Whoever comes to them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they will not return him; and whoever comes to us from them, we return him to them; and that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come the next year with his Companions and enter Mecca as pilgrims, staying only three days, and bringing only carried arms — the sword, the bow, and the like."
"18888","Narrated to us Husayn ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carrying the soil of the Trench until the soil covered the skin of his belly, while he chanted the words of Abdullah ibn Rawaha: O Allah, were it not for You we would not be guided, nor give charity, nor pray. So send down tranquility upon us, and make firm the feet when we meet. Indeed the foremost have wronged us, and if they want trial, we refuse."
"18889","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Shu'ba from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: A silk suit was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his Companions began to touch it and marvel at its softness. So he said: Do you marvel at the softness of this. The handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better than it, or softer."
"18890","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar, he said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa narrating from al-Bara that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he woke up, would say: Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection. Shu'ba said: This or something like this in meaning. And when he slept, he would say: O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die."
"18891","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz, Shu'ba narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said concerning his son Ibrahim: He has a nursing mother in Paradise."
"18892","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Adi — Bahz said: Adi ibn Thabit narrated to us — he said: I heard al-Bara — and Bahz said: From al-Bara ibn Azib — saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and he prayed the last Isha, and recited in one of the two rak'as: By the fig and the olive."
"18893","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Adi — Bahz said: Adi ibn Thabit informed us — he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan ibn Thabit: Attack them, or lampoon them, and Jibril is with you. Bahz said: Lampoon them, and attack them, or he said: Lampoon them, or attack them."
"18894","Narrated to us Affan, narrated to us Shu'ba, Adi ibn Thabit informed us, he said: I heard al-Bara saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Hassan: Lampoon them, or attack them, and Jibril is with you."
"18895","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Shu'ba from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Abu Juhayfa from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: Abu Burda slaughtered before the prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Replace it. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have only a jadha'a, and I think he said: Better than a musinna. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make it in its place, but it will never suffice for anyone after you."
"18896","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Shu'ba from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, he said: I heard al-Bara narrating to a people among whom was Ka'b ibn Ujra, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he opened the prayer, raise his hands."
"18897","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Shu'ba from Zubayd al-Iyami from al-Sha'bi from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing we begin with on this day of ours is that we pray, then we return and slaughter. So whoever does that has hit our sunna, and whoever slaughters, then it is only meat he offered to his family; it is nothing of the rite. He said: And Abu Burda ibn Niyar had slaughtered, so he said: I have a jadha'a better than a musinna. So he said: Slaughter it, but it will never suffice for anyone after you."
"18898","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Awf from Maymun Abu Abdullah from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to dig the Trench. He said: And a rock appeared to us in a place in the Trench that picks would not take. He said: So they complained of it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came — Awf said: And I think he said: He put down his garment, then descended to the rock and took the pick. So he said: In the name of Allah, and struck a blow, and broke a third of the stone, and said: Allah is greatest; I have been given the keys of Sham. By Allah, I indeed see its red palaces from this place of mine. Then he said: In the name of Allah, and struck another, and broke a third of the stone, and said: Allah is greatest; I have been given the keys of Persia. By Allah, I indeed see al-Mada'in, and I see its white palace from this place of mine. Then he said: In the name of Allah, and struck another blow, and uprooted the rest of the stone, and said: Allah is greatest; I have been given the keys of Yemen. By Allah, I indeed see the gates of Sanaa from this place of mine."
"18899","Narrated to us Hawdha, narrated to us Awf from Maymun, he said: Al-Bara ibn Azib al-Ansari informed me, then he mentioned it."
"18900","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Yusuf, narrated to us Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), at his sleep, would place his right hand under his cheek and say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants."
"18901","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Hassan ibn Thabit: Lampoon the polytheists, for Jibril is with you."
"18902","Yazid and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said: Yahya narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: Yazid said: Adi ibn Thabit informed him that al-Bara ibn Azib informed him that he prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Isha prayer, Ibn Numayr said: the last, and he recited therein At-Tin wal-Zaytun."
"18903","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Ajlah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No two Muslims meet and shake hands except they are forgiven before they part."
"18904","Yala narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I never saw any man at all more handsome than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a red hullah."
"18905","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that he described the prostration, he said: He spread his palms, raised his buttocks, drew his arms apart from his sides, and said: Thus the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrated."
"18906","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he said the takbir, would raise his hands until we saw his thumbs near his ears."
"18907","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: Do we pray in the resting places of camels He said: No. He said: Do we pray in the resting places of sheep He said: Yes. He said: Do we perform ablution from camel meat He said: Yes. He said: Do we perform ablution from sheep meat He said: No. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abdullah ibn Abdullah is Razi, and he was the judge of al-Rayy, and his grandmother was a freed slave of Ali or a slave girl, and Adam and Said ibn Masruq narrated from him, and he was trustworthy."
"18908","Yahya and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, Ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Talhah al-Yami, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever grants a grant of silver, or guides through an alley, or gives milk to drink, for him is the equivalent of freeing a slave or a soul."
"18909","And whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, ten times, for him is the equivalent of freeing a slave or a soul."
"18910","And he would come to us when we stood for prayer and wipe our chests or our shoulders, saying: Do not let your rows differ, lest your hearts differ. And he would say: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row, or the first rows."
"18911","And he said: Beautify the Quran with your voices. I had forgotten it, then al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim reminded me of it."
"18912","Yahya narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to me, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from al-Bara, he said: Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, or a son of his, a son of sixteen months, while an infant. Yahya said: I think it is Ibrahim, upon him prayer and peace. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He has a nursing mother who will complete his nursing in Paradise."
"18913","Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: A man said to him: O Abu Umarah, did you turn back on the day of Hunayn He said: No, by Allah, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not turn back, but the hasty ones among the people turned back. Hawazin met them with arrows, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a white mule, and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith was holding its bridle, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was saying: I am the Prophet, no lie, I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib."
"18914","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months or seventeen months, then he was turned toward the Kabah, and he loved that. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: We see the turning of your face toward heaven, so We shall turn you to a qiblah that pleases you, so turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Haram, the verse. He said: Then a man who had prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Asr prayer passed by some people of the Ansar while they were bowing in the Asr prayer toward Bayt al-Maqdis. He said, testifying that he had prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and that he had been turned toward the Kabah. He said: So they turned aside while bowing in the Asr prayer."
"18915","Waki narrated to us, from Misar, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reciting in the Isha prayer, Muhammad said: At-Tin wal-Zaytun."
"18916","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr informed us, al-Amash, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Beautify the Quran with your voices."
"18917","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he raised his head from bowing, none of us would bend his back until he prostrated, then we would prostrate."
"18918","Waki narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from Ibn al-Bara, from al-Bara, he said: When we prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among what we loved, or we love, was to stand on his right, and I heard him saying: My Lord, save me from Your punishment on the day You gather Your servants, or resurrect Your servants."
"18919","Waki narrated to us, Abu Janab narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Bara, from his father al-Bara, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivered a sermon leaning on a bow or a staff."
